WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.353 --> 00:00:11.700
Blackheads and clogged ears

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.510
can be super uncomfortable,

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.470
but it's important to leave any picking

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.810
and prodding to the experts.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.500
This is how professionals treat

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.497
and clean five body parts,

00:00:21.497 --> 00:00:26.123
including the teeth, scalp, and toenails.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.060
This teeth-cleaning method

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.820
is called guided biofilm therapy, or GBT.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.423
The goal is to remove
biofilm from the teeth.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:40.840
It's a layer of bacteria

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.210
that's responsible for
bleeding gums, bad breath,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.723
and some dental infections and diseases.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.860
Unlike plaque, you can't
see or feel biofilm

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.900
because it's so tiny.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.220
That's why dental hygienist Faye Donald

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.960
is painting each tooth
with this purple liquid.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.552
It's an organic colored dye

00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:02.502
called Biofilm Discloser.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.250
It stains early biofilm,

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.820
which is less than three days old, pink

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.311
and mature biofilm,

00:01:09.311 --> 00:01:12.540
which is more than three days old, blue.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.920
Donald wants to disrupt early biofilm

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.393
before it has the chance
to mature into plaque.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.263
Now the cleaning process begins.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.530
She's using a tool called Airflow Max,

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.830
which acts like a gentle
jet wash inside the mouth.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:30.462
It uses a combination of warm water

00:01:30.462 --> 00:01:33.310
and soluble antimicrobial powder.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:36.683
Donald says it'll remove
100% of the biofilm

00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:39.920
from the teeth, even
in the dark, warm areas

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.060
that the biofilm likes to hide.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.693
It also removes stains.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.430
Now that that's done,

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:53.090
she uses a descaling kit
called Piezon No Pain.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.330
It uses ultrasonic vibrations

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:58.260
to remove any remaining
hard buildup or plaque

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.660
from the teeth.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.810
Unlike old plaque-removal methods,

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.530
there is no scraping involved,

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:06.553
so it won't scratch or
damage the tooth's surface.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.136
Earwax can be soupy, hard,

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.900
crumbly, soft, and even moldy.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:23.325
Professionals will scrape, suck,

00:02:23.325 --> 00:02:24.725
or flush it out.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.750
The removal method depends on

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.450
the consistency of the wax

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.660
and where it's located
inside the ear canal.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.480
Here, we're looking at hard, impacted wax.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.921
But this wax is way too impacted,

00:02:37.921 --> 00:02:40.204
so suction isn't working.

00:02:40.204 --> 00:02:42.890
He switches to a Cawthorne hook No. 6,

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.498
which is a tiny metal right-angle hook

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.830
with a pointy end.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.521
It's so small that Boland

00:02:49.521 --> 00:02:51.804
can maneuver the hook around the debris

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.993
and gently dig it out of the ear canal.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.930
It's important that he carefully digs

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.360
and scrapes out the debris in stages.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.233
Otherwise, painful damage
to the ear can occur.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.890
The wax became like this
after the patient tried

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.333
to self-treat it with water-based drops.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.375
Earwax is important for ear health,

00:03:40.375 --> 00:03:43.080
so Boland says that it
should only ever be removed

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.480
if it's bothering the patient.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.713
And in that case,

00:03:46.713 --> 00:03:48.321
it's important to visit a specialist

00:03:48.321 --> 00:03:50.063
to get it professionally removed.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.410
Felicia Brown created a
holistic scalp cleanse

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.200
for clients with serious dandruff buildup.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.930
To prep the scalp, she
sprays the cleansing product

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.470
directly on the client's head.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:09.611
Now she's scratching

00:04:09.611 --> 00:04:11.436
and freeing the scalp of dandruff,

00:04:11.436 --> 00:04:14.063
dead skin, and anything
else that's clogging it.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.440
Once the buildup is
removed, she sprays the hair

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.160
with the cleansing product again

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.800
and lets it sit for 15 to 20 minutes.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.563
The scalp is shampooed
and thoroughly massaged.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.975
She says clients usually experience

00:04:33.975 --> 00:04:36.740
immediate relief after the treatment.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.750
The scalp cleanse was made for patients

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:42.043
with psoriasis, eczema, dermatitis,

00:04:42.043 --> 00:04:44.363
dandruff, or a clogged scalp.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.170
Lori Halloway is a nail technician

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:53.010
who cleans thick, impacted toenails.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.585
She starts by soaking the feet

00:04:54.585 --> 00:04:56.276
in a whirlpool foot bath

00:04:56.276 --> 00:04:59.010
that contains foot soap and foot salt.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:01.510
This helps soften and disinfect the skin

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:03.850
and loosen up the debris.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.508
She treats the bottom of the foot

00:05:05.508 --> 00:05:07.041
with a callus remover.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.080
Nail nippers reduce the
length of the toenail,

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.570
and a cuticle pusher pushes back the skin

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.283
that's stuck to the nail plate.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.350
She uses an ingrown-toenail
sidewall cleaner

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:24.230
to carefully pull out all
of the impacted debris

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.803
from the sides and underneath the toenail.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.330
She often uses an electric file

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.333
to reduce the thickness of the nail.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.530
When a toenail is too thick,

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:38.010
it hits the top and front of the shoe.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.710
This is what causes it to grow abnormally,

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:43.223
which can lead to infection or injury.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.540
Claudia Colombo is an esthetician

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.473
who professionally performs
blackhead extractions.

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.890
Before the extraction process begins,

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:57.670
she massages the face
to drain the lymph nodes

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.423
and gently cleanses the skin.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.580
Then she pre-softens the
skin with a warm towel

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.330
and an enzyme treatment.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.305
This makes it easier for the blackheads

00:06:07.305 --> 00:06:08.488
to be extracted.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.675
That silver spatula is actually

00:06:16.675 --> 00:06:18.541
an ultrasonic skin scrubber,

00:06:18.541 --> 00:06:21.840
which Colombo uses to exfoliate the skin.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.900
The ultrasonic waves help loosen

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.503
and remove oil and dirt from the pores.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.590
She starts gently
extracting the blackheads

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:33.663
with her fingers.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.740
Not much pressure is needed,

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:41.823
since the skin has already
been prepped and softened.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.610
It's important to replenish the skin

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.200
with minerals and nutrients

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.750
that may have been lost
during the process.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.360
In this case, Colombo
applies some chlorophyll

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:03.240
and copper complex to replenish magnesium

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.743
and copper in the skin.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.858
She leaves it to incubate

00:07:11.858 --> 00:07:15.100
and then applies a blue
light to help heal the skin.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.060
The light also allows the ingredients

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.820
to penetrate deeper into the pores.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.295
Lastly, she applies a hydro jelly mask

00:07:22.295 --> 00:07:23.561
to soothe the skin.

